  "doc_revision": "SITRANS F Communication Modules Modbus RTU RS 485 Operating Instructions, 03/2021, A5E00753974-AB (FDK-085U0234)",
  "verified": false,
  "notes": "Register map is Appendix A and B of the add-on module manual (also covers MASS 6000, product code 25; only the MAG 6000 tables were used; the MASS 6000 process-data layout differs and is not in this preset). Tables list both a 'MODBUS register' (4:03003) and a 'MODBUS address' (3002); the manual's own example reads 'absolute massflow (4:03001)' with start address 0x0BB8 = 3000, so the frame address is the second column. address_base=0 and 'address' is that MODBUS address column. Data are big-endian; floats are IEEE 754 with the high word first (manual example 100.0 = 42C80000 in registers N, N+1), doubles occupy 4 registers; 'Byte' type values live in the low byte of one register. Only FC01, 03, 05, 16 (and 17) are supported; reads use FC03 for all registers (holding register area, 4:). Engineering units of flow/totalizer follow the unit registers (default m3/s and m3), exposed as separate enum points; values carry no hard-coded unit. Unit IDs were transcribed from a table with a garbled text layer. Factory communication settings stated in Table 5-1: address 1, 19200 baud, Even parity 1 stop bit, response delay 0, interframe space 3.5 chars. Writable settings are marked rw; they affect scaling/outputs of the meter (Q max, low flow cut-off, flow direction) or the link itself (address, baud) - handle with care. Totalizer reset/hold coils are plain coil writes and are in group 'control'. Left out: zero adjust (only on MAG 6000 SV, calibration), current/pulse/relay output setup, batch, service info, TAG and other strings, restart-Modbus coil, auto-zero start coil (0:00009).",
